yer of grid equipment in Caldria (`utility-capex-2027`).\n- **Pellham's equity raise failed.** It withdrew a C$2.4B offering because investor demand fell short. It is now cutting 2027 transformer orders by about 40% and deferring two substation programmes \"until financing improves\" (`pellham-offering`).\n- **Equity is weak across the sector.** Two other utility share offerings were cut back in size (`utility-credit`, Q3 2026).\n- **Debt is open but costlier.** Bond spreads widened 30bp to 165bp in Q3. Norvane still priced a C$1.1B bond comfortably (`utility-credit`).\n\n**Implications**\n- Utilities that rely on equity face resizing or deferral. Pellham has already shown this by cutting capex.\n- Utilities that rely on debt can still fund, at higher cost. Norvane's raise supports this, but one deal is thin evidence.\n- For grid-equipment demand, the equity shortfall is a real downside risk. Pellham's order cut is concrete, and it is the largest buyer.\n\n**Gaps:** The sources give no data on utilities' balance-sheet headroom, equity valuations, or whether the market might reopen. I did not check how much of the capex plan is meant to be equity-funded, or how much Norvane needs to raise.","ttft_ms":2390,"type":"result","duration_ms":20074,"uuid":"44957a5a-c640-418e-9f86-ab82caba5cf1","ttft_stream_ms":1886,"time_to_request_ms":66,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":5,"system_prompt":8,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":9,"input_attachments":11,"input_hooks":1,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":2,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":5,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":2,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":5,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":2,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":2,"request_build":4},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":16,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":55,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_st